<title>UK: UK's Clarke says to stem tax loopholes.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says to stem tax loopholes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday that his budget will propose measures to stem tax loopholes</p>
<p>&quot;I will propose a number of measures to stem tax leakage, to protect the ordinary tax payer,&quot; he said in a speech to Parliament on the 1997/98 budget, &quot;and make sure we get the right tax from the right people.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;When I reduce tax I want to do so in a way that is fair for business and fair for the hard working British man and woman,&quot; Clarke added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
